---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Photographer"
  description="Meet Caleb, the photographer behind Bitterroot Boudoir in Stevensville, Montana."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap photographer">
      <div class="bio">
        <h1 class="reveal">Meet Caleb</h1>
        <p class="subheader reveal reveal-delay-1">Your Photographer</p>

        <div class="bio-copy reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <p>
            I began my photographic journey in the wild, photographing landscapes
            and the natural world around me. Nature photography taught me how to
            study a subject and discover how light can reveal moments of quiet
            drama and breathtaking beauty. I learned that a photographer’s job
            isn’t to create beauty, but rather to find what’s already there and
            honor it through light and perspective.
          </p>
          <p>
            For me, boudoir is no different. Every body is its own unique
            landscape, shaped by curves, lines, and stories. When light falls
            just right, it reveals an elegance that can be emotionally
            moving.
          </p>
          <p>
            My goal is to help you fall in love with your own image — not just
            with a favorite photo or two, but with the person in them. Hearing
            that I’ve played a small part in helping a client feel better about
            themselves and leave a session more confident is indescribably
            rewarding.
          </p>
          <p>
            There's beauty in all of us, and we all owe it to ourselves to
            discover it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cta-stack reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Contact</a>
          <details class="more-about">
            <summary class="more-about-toggle">More about me</summary>
            <div class="more-about-body">
              <p>
                I live just outside of Stevensville, Montana with my beautiful wife
                Cheri (that's her at the top of my homepage!) and our mischievous cat
                Winkis (no, I did not name him). It was actually Cheri who encouraged
                me to begin offering my boudoir photo services publicly. After doing
                professional-level sessions with her and a number of our friends, she
                told me, "Everyone should do this. Everyone should feel this good
                about themselves." I agree.
              </p>
              <p>
                Outside of boudoir, I am still a passionate nature and landscape
                photographer, and you may find me trudging up our local trails chasing
                daybreak or storm clouds with camera in tow. The outdoors are in our
                blood, and my wife and I spend as much time as we can hiking, fishing,
                camping, foraging, and generally frolicking in nature.
              </p>
              <p>
                Educationally, I have a degree in Aerospace Engineering (sounds fancy,
                eh?). I still use my background practically and creatively by designing
                small products and solving problems for a few companies. Mostly, the
                technical background has enhanced my knowledge and appreciation for the
                more complex aspects of my endeavors. Be careful when asking me too much
                about the technical components of photography, cameras, lenses, or
                software… I tend to lose myself in it.
              </p>
              <p>
                Some will ask me what it's like being a male photographer in the boudoir
                genre. Really, it's the same as anyone pursuing any other form of art.
                Both my wife and I are artists in different mediums, and we both have a
                great appreciation for the human form. I don't see the gender of the
                photographer as being important in capturing a photo, but I also
                understand some clients would prefer a same-gender photographer for more
                intimate photography, and I can respect that. My goal is to perform my
                job as a professional, ensure every client has as good an experience as
                possible, and do my best to provide a comfortable and respectful
                environment for everyone.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <img
        class="portrait reveal reveal-delay-3"
        src="/images/about/photographer.webp"
        alt="Caleb, photographer at Bitterroot Boudoir"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .photographer {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .portrait {
    width: min(100%, 26rem);
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .subheader {
    margin: -0.35em 0 1.25em;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .bio-copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1em;
  }

  .bio-copy p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cta-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .more-about {
    width: min(100%, 36rem);
  }

  .more-about-toggle {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 0;
    padding: 0.2rem 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(181, 169, 160, 0.45);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    transition: color 0.25s var(--ease), text-decoration-color 0.25s var(--ease);
  }

  .more-about-toggle::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .more-about-toggle:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .more-about[open] .more-about-toggle {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.55);
  }

  .more-about-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1em;
    margin-top: 1.15rem;
    padding-top: 1.15rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .more-about-body p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .photographer {
      grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }

    .portrait {
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 1rem);
    }
  }
</style>
